WEBVTT

00:29:58.327 --> 00:30:00.433
that they already have
some intuitive skills

00:30:00.457 --> 00:30:02.526
for building rapid
high-quality connections.

00:30:02.550 --> 00:30:03.837
But can it work somewhere

00:30:03.861 --> 00:30:06.156
where colleagues tend
to keep to themselves?

00:30:06.180 --> 00:30:08.736
To find out, we went
to a coworking space in New York

00:30:08.760 --> 00:30:10.816
called PencilWorks.

00:30:10.840 --> 00:30:13.856
At PencilWorks, it's been a struggle
to bring people together.

00:30:13.880 --> 00:30:16.226
The building's community
manager, Nathan Windsor,

00:30:16.250 --> 00:30:18.446
has been grappling with this for a while.

00:30:18.470 --> 00:30:22.310
Nathan Windsor: I mean, we've run 
game nights here every Friday for years,

00:30:22.334 --> 00:30:23.570
and people don't show up.

00:30:23.594 --> 00:30:27.686
And we do happy hours,
and people don't show up.

00:30:27.710 --> 00:30:29.696
Everyone is really in their own office.

00:30:29.720 --> 00:30:31.676
They're really in their own head